1
00:00:00,913 --> 00:00:05,240
dicizado, seaguca,

2
00:00:05,340 --> 00:00:11,917
senori,

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,780
small tea .Full speed at the train,

4
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:23,120
keep going on for no police,
don't forget to play?

5
00:00:31,180 --> 00:00:33,980
Let's go.

6
00:01:05,240 --> 00:01:06,557
I'll

7
00:01:06,640 --> 00:01:07,957
see

8
00:01:08,040 --> 00:01:13,677
you

9
00:01:13,760 --> 00:01:20,760
next

10
00:01:22,940 --> 00:01:23,770
time.

11
00:01:30,080 --> 00:01:33,433
It was great meeting Mimi,
who was visiting from America.

12
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:34,740
She's so glamorous.

13
00:01:34,860 --> 00:01:38,217
We all decided to spend our Saturday
picnicking in the digital world.

14
00:01:38,300 --> 00:01:40,837
Everything was going great,
except for the food fight,

15
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:42,837
when some of us got
separated and fell into a

16
00:01:42,920 --> 00:01:45,820
new area that was controlled
by a control spire.

17
00:01:46,020 --> 00:01:48,277
That's why the Gekkomon
didn't remember Mimi.

18
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:51,217
But luckily, Palmon remembered
her and saved us from them.

19
00:01:51,300 --> 00:01:53,177
They were happy to see each other,

20
00:01:53,260 --> 00:01:55,337
but we weren't happy to
see the Roachmon brothers.

21
00:01:55,420 --> 00:01:58,517
However, we made them destroy
the Control Spire for us.

22
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:00,071
I wish Mimi were staying.

23
00:02:00,180 --> 00:02:02,121
I almost feel like we're sisters.

24
00:02:06,820 --> 00:02:08,060
Daddy no kyo-ku.

25
00:02:10,180 --> 00:02:11,010
Ta-da!

26
00:02:13,460 --> 00:02:14,290
Yeah!

27
00:02:16,460 --> 00:02:19,460
All right, that's 12 more
Control Spires destroyed.

28
00:02:22,440 --> 00:02:23,270
Yeah!

29
00:02:25,180 --> 00:02:26,337
According to the map,

30
00:02:26,420 --> 00:02:29,957
Greymon has finished in this area
and is moving on to the next.

31
00:02:30,040 --> 00:02:32,040
Gorillamon's doing the same thing.

32
00:02:33,660 --> 00:02:36,817
There's still one more control
spire to destroy today.

33
00:02:36,900 --> 00:02:38,777
Maybe Greymon could get that one too.

34
00:02:38,860 --> 00:02:40,095
I don't think he can.

35
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:42,277
It looks like he's too far from that area.

36
00:02:42,360 --> 00:02:43,190
Ty's right.

37
00:02:43,360 --> 00:02:45,478
In that case, we'll do it ourselves.

38
00:02:54,460 --> 00:02:56,060
I am Gardromon,

39
00:02:56,280 --> 00:02:57,897
whoever tries to enter the premises shall

40
00:02:57,980 --> 00:03:00,457
become victims of my
grenade destroyer attack.

41
00:03:00,540 --> 00:03:01,660
Gold Rush!

42
00:03:03,220 --> 00:03:04,360
Star Shower!

43
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:07,780
Fire Rocket!

44
00:03:09,760 --> 00:03:11,080
Intruder, Intruder!

45
00:03:11,460 --> 00:03:13,057
There must be a hundred of them!

46
00:03:13,140 --> 00:03:16,937
Wow, you counted that high without
even taking off your shoes and socks.

47
00:03:17,020 --> 00:03:19,837
I think now's a good time
to go back to our world.

48
00:03:19,920 --> 00:03:21,477
We can come up with a new plan.

49
00:03:21,560 --> 00:03:22,390
TK's right.

50
00:03:22,473 --> 00:03:23,616
We can talk to Izzy.

51
00:03:24,620 --> 00:03:25,960
Intruder! Intruder!

52
00:03:26,420 --> 00:03:28,840
Are you guys out of your minds? Quit now!

53
00:03:29,020 --> 00:03:30,457
I've never been a quitter!

54
00:03:30,540 --> 00:03:31,370
I agree.

55
00:03:31,453 --> 00:03:32,595
Davis, let's regroup.

56
00:03:35,140 --> 00:03:36,787
Davis, don't be so stubborn.

57
00:03:36,980 --> 00:03:38,237
There are far too many of them.

58
00:03:38,320 --> 00:03:40,377
We have to get out of here while we can.

59
00:03:40,460 --> 00:03:42,060
I agree. We have to hurry.

60
00:03:45,460 --> 00:03:47,980
All right, head for the gate!

61
00:03:50,760 --> 00:03:51,740
Digiport, open!

62
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:02,997
Grenade destroyer!

63
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:03,910
Wait for me!

64
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:08,310
Ouch!

65
00:04:08,393 --> 00:04:10,757
Say, shouldn't we put pillows here
if we're going to keep doing this?

66
00:04:10,840 --> 00:04:15,277
Guys, I saw that the TV was blown up as
we came through, so we can't go back.

67
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:16,190
Wait a second.

68
00:04:16,420 --> 00:04:17,479
Where did Kari go?

69
00:04:17,780 --> 00:04:18,660
She's trapped.

70
00:04:18,980 --> 00:04:20,340
In the digital world.

71
00:04:24,580 --> 00:04:26,639
I don't think this has spell check.

72
00:04:27,080 --> 00:04:32,140
Kari, if we find ourselves in any kind
of jam, I can always arm or digivolve.

73
00:04:32,340 --> 00:04:34,937
Well, let's save that
for a special occasion.

74
00:04:35,020 --> 00:04:36,920
The gate to that area is closed.

75
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:38,296
We can't get to her.

76
00:04:38,940 --> 00:04:39,770
D .K.,

77
00:04:39,853 --> 00:04:43,037
wasn't Kari right behind you when you
went into the gate from the digital world?

78
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:43,950
Mm-hmm.

79
00:04:44,033 --> 00:04:44,997
Then it's all your fault.

80
00:04:45,080 --> 00:04:47,320
Why didn't you let her go first? Stop.

81
00:04:47,580 --> 00:04:48,677
It was no one's fault.

82
00:04:48,760 --> 00:04:49,597
It just happened.

83
00:04:49,680 --> 00:04:50,510
What do you know?

84
00:04:50,593 --> 00:04:51,457
You're a little kid.

85
00:04:51,540 --> 00:04:54,540
Yeah, but I still know when
someone's being a jerk.

86
00:04:55,360 --> 00:04:56,700
Oh, I guess that's me.

87
00:04:56,940 --> 00:04:59,320
Truth is, Davis is right. Huh?

88
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:02,140
It really was my fault.

89
00:05:02,440 --> 00:05:05,381
I should have been watching
out for her all along.

90
00:05:05,980 --> 00:05:08,140
Well, I guess I could have, too.

91
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:09,320
So could I.

92
00:05:09,620 --> 00:05:10,738
That's what I mean.

93
00:05:10,920 --> 00:05:12,520
There's no one to blame.

94
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:14,310
Huh?

95
00:05:14,780 --> 00:05:17,680
Hey, guys, it's an email from Kari. Huh?

96
00:05:18,060 --> 00:05:22,037
It says, don't worry, I'm all right, and
I'm sorry if any words are misspelled.

97
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:23,061
Sincerely, Kari.

98
00:05:23,520 --> 00:05:24,857
Yoli, I've got an idea.

99
00:05:24,940 --> 00:05:28,597
If I can find an area close to the
one she's in, then I can reach her.

100
00:05:28,680 --> 00:05:29,510
Got it.

101
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:31,480
I'll be back soon.

102
00:05:31,820 --> 00:05:32,820
I'm going soon.

103
00:05:34,880 --> 00:05:35,777
What should we do?

104
00:05:35,860 --> 00:05:40,389
If he thinks I'm going to stand by and
let him be the hero, he can forget it.

105
00:05:40,880 --> 00:05:41,710
What?

106
00:05:41,793 --> 00:05:42,623
Then I'm going.

107
00:05:42,706 --> 00:05:43,757
Yoli, wait a minute.

108
00:05:43,840 --> 00:05:46,057
Listen, it's almost dinner time right now.

109
00:05:46,140 --> 00:05:48,337
Somewhere between the green
salad and the green gelatin,

110
00:05:48,420 --> 00:05:50,577
