to wonder where they are.

111
00:05:50,660 --> 00:05:52,657
We have to tell Tai and the others.

112
00:05:52,740 --> 00:05:56,997
I think that's the best thing you and I
can do to help Davis and TK right now.

113
00:05:57,080 --> 00:05:58,457
Cody, I know you're just a kid,

114
00:05:58,540 --> 00:06:01,097
but sometimes you have the
wisdom of an old man of 20.

115
00:06:01,180 --> 00:06:02,877
All right, what are we waiting for?

116
00:06:02,960 --> 00:06:03,790
Let's go.

117
00:06:03,873 --> 00:06:05,831
But wait, you can't just go out in public.

118
00:06:06,640 --> 00:06:10,097
This was a great idea, crossing
the desert without any water.

119
00:06:10,180 --> 00:06:11,937
Look, I didn't ask for your help.

120
00:06:12,020 --> 00:06:13,020
There's the city!

121
00:06:14,180 --> 00:06:17,217
Looks like one of those things
you shake and it starts snowing.

122
00:06:17,300 --> 00:06:18,257
I'll go get Kari.

123
00:06:18,340 --> 00:06:19,170
You wait here.

124
00:06:19,253 --> 00:06:20,420
No, I'll get Kari.

125
00:06:20,580 --> 00:06:21,560
You wait here.

126
00:06:21,880 --> 00:06:23,097
All right, I'll tell you what.

127
00:06:23,180 --> 00:06:24,300
We'll flip for it.

128
00:06:24,440 --> 00:06:26,240
Winner goes, loser stays here.

129
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:29,380
Since it's my coin, I
get to call it. Tails.

130
00:06:31,100 --> 00:06:33,460
Okay, if it's tails, I rescue Kari.

131
00:06:33,700 --> 00:06:35,406
If it's heads, you get to go.

132
00:06:37,100 --> 00:06:37,930
Tails!

133
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:41,397
I'll tell her that you were
worried about her and that you...

134
00:06:41,480 --> 00:06:44,120
Huh, a coin that has tails on both sides.

135
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:46,504
That's how I used to beat Matt.

136
00:06:46,780 --> 00:06:47,662
How about that?

137
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:50,900
Let's both go.

138
00:06:53,100 --> 00:06:56,197
Okay, TM, did you really use
one of those coins on Matt?

139
00:06:56,280 --> 00:07:00,045
Yeah, that's how I got all my
baseball cards and his old guitar.

140
00:07:01,940 --> 00:07:05,020
TK and Davis sure argue a lot. How come?

141
00:07:05,280 --> 00:07:06,580
Something about Kari.

142
00:07:06,840 --> 00:07:09,546
Human girls make human
boys act sort of weird.

143
00:07:12,200 --> 00:07:14,360
Intruder! Intruder! Intruder!

144
00:07:15,660 --> 00:07:16,680
Rosetta Stone!

145
00:07:20,640 --> 00:07:23,287
Kari, there aren't any
TVs left in this area.

146
00:07:23,640 --> 00:07:26,287
We'll have to go to
another area to find one.

147
00:07:26,460 --> 00:07:29,342
But we don't even know
which direction to travel.

148
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:32,620
It's almost your dinner time.

149
00:07:32,840 --> 00:07:35,075
Shouldn't you be going home soon, Ken?

150
00:07:36,620 --> 00:07:39,000
Never calling anything but master!

151
00:07:42,580 --> 00:07:44,900
Since she's all alone,

152
00:07:46,260 --> 00:07:48,360
she deserves someone special.

153
00:07:51,640 --> 00:07:53,360
Oh, no, you can't.

154
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:54,820
Anyone but him.

155
00:07:58,900 --> 00:07:59,730
Hello?

156
00:07:59,813 --> 00:08:00,969
Can I speak to Tai, please?

157
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:03,146
No, I'm not selling anything.

158
00:08:04,080 --> 00:08:04,980
You know, Yoli,

159
00:08:05,240 --> 00:08:07,597
with all the snacks and drinks
you take to give your friends,

160
00:08:07,680 --> 00:08:10,137
it's a wonder this store
shows any profit at all.

161
00:08:10,220 --> 00:08:11,437
Put it on my tab, Daddy.

162
00:08:11,520 --> 00:08:13,402
So that's where Kari is now, Tai.

163
00:08:13,940 --> 00:08:14,770
Okay, Cody.

164
00:08:14,940 --> 00:08:16,137
Thanks for letting me know.

165
00:08:16,220 --> 00:08:17,197
Don't worry about it.

166
00:08:17,280 --> 00:08:18,986
I'll take care of everything.

167
00:08:21,540 --> 00:08:24,037
Kari's at a friend's house doing
a science project on gravity,

168
00:08:24,120 --> 00:08:26,377
and they need to see how
long I can stand on my head.

169
00:08:26,460 --> 00:08:27,290
See ya!

170
00:08:27,560 --> 00:08:28,390
Huh?

171
00:08:28,473 --> 00:08:29,303
Hey, Tai, I heard what happened.

172
00:08:29,386 --> 00:08:30,216
So, are you going to go?

173
00:08:30,299 --> 00:08:31,317
Yeah, in a few minutes.

174
00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:33,777
But first, I have to make
a stop by Davis' apartment.

175
00:08:33,860 --> 00:08:35,557
I have to make up a
story to tell his family

176
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:37,297
